Provenance / clean-room statement
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OpenDogShow is an independent, clean-room implementation.

- Its domain model, terminology, rules, and interfaces are derived from
  PRIMARY kennel-club regulations (notably the FCI Regulations for Dog Shows
  and the regulations of the Belgian FCI member, the Société Royale
  Saint-Hubert / Koninklijke Maatschappij Sint-Hubertus), and from original
  work. Research is cited to its primary sources and preserved on the
  `research/*` branches under `docs/research/`.

- No source code, user-interface text, screenshots, page layouts, database
  contents, or other copyrightable EXPRESSION of any competing product has
  been copied, reproduced, or reverse-engineered in the creation of this
  project. Any resemblance in features or functionality reflects the shared,
  factual real-world domain (running conformation dog shows), which is not
  subject to copyright.

- Facts, ideas, and functionality are not owned; a competitor's specific
  expression is. Contributors attest to respecting this distinction via the
  Developer Certificate of Origin and the anti-copy policy in CONTRIBUTING.md.

